From bba04484d71035760547a987b372edca3d13f64f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khunmax2 <khuncharoenmax1@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:03:22 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(maic): let a server TTS provider declare its voices;
 translate the editor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two findings the UAT reported rather than fixed.

server-providers.yml carried no TTS at all — 1 LLM, 0 TTS, 1 ASR — so speech
worked on the one browser that had configured it by hand and nowhere else,
because TTS settings live in a per-browser store. The bridge emitted nothing
because ServerProviderEntry had apiKey, baseUrl, models, proxy and no voice: an
engine whose only voice is dr_wit, mapped onto the built-in openai-tts, was
called with `alloy` and refused. Emitting nothing beat emitting that, but it
left a new user with a course and no narration.

`voices:` mirrors `models:` — declared in YAML or ${PREFIX}_VOICES, carried
through the same merge, authoritative over the client's choice via a new
resolveTTSVoice, and surfaced to the picker so the UI stops offering a voice the
request will never use. loadEnvSection needed it too: it copied four named
fields, so an unlisted one was dropped on the floor.

Verified from a browser with cleared storage: 1 TTS loaded,
/api/server-providers returns {"openai-tts":{"voices":["dr_wit"]}}, and course
generation made 9 TTS calls, all voice=dr_wit, zero errors.

The slide editor's context menus were Chinese — all 43: cut/copy/paste, the
align and layer submenus, grid and ruler, the line presets. Empirically
unreachable today (the editor flag is off and no edit affordance exists in the
classroom) but one env var from being the whole right-click menu. 37 keys under
editor.menu.*, 13 languages, wired through t().

Two hid in ternary else-branches (组合, 直线) where a sweep for quoted literals in
a menu table does not look — the same shape as the Play/Pause labels earlier
today. A literal-only grep is not a sufficient check for hardcoded copy.

tsc clean, eslint clean, i18n gate 13 locales, tests/server 377 passed with 6
pre-existing 5s timeouts and no assertion failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
